{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792530986559,"sessionID":"ses_ea4d52decffeaHsc6A3RWeHtGB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_4J7Jb6NAQzobbS7bWFPa9388","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\variants\\a\\src\\geocache-milestone-card.ts","offset":540,"limit":75},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\variants\\a\\src\\geocache-milestone-card.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n540: const WHY: WhySpec = {\n541:   \"day\": 31,\n542:   \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n543:   \"agent\": \"opencode\",\n544:   \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-pro\",\n545:   \"id\": \"@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\",\n546:   \"title\": \"Geocache Milestone Card\",\n547:   \"who\": \"Geocachers hitting a milestone or building a stats card, gathered on the Geocaching forums, Project-GC, and their local clubs\",\n548:   \"problem\": [\n549:     \"Every Premium member can download their My Finds pocket query: a zipped GPX of every cache they logged. Project-GC's Milestones tab gives the ladder: 'the first milestones are 1, 10, 50 and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is considered a milestone'.\",\n550:     \"CacheSleuth reads the same GPX into a profile banner ('Upload your My Finds pocket query and see your geocaching statistics'), but the shareable 'I hit N finds' card is still hand-built; a local club just posts 'geohiker55 found his 1000th find yesterday'.\"\n551:   ],\n552:   \"sources\": [\n553:     \"https://www.cachesleuth.com/tools/profilestats\",\n554:     \"https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab\",\n555:     \"https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2025/05/celebrating-25-years-of-geocaching-milestones\",\n556:     \"https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page\",\n557:     \"https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\"\n558:   ],\n559:   \"solution\": [\n560:     \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n561:     \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The card derives the ordinal (1,000th) and whether the count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about.\"\n562:   ],\n563:   \"usage\": {\n564:     \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @card.json -o card.png\",\n565:     \"try\": [\n566:       \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}]}\",\n567:       \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print it (Project-GC milestones)\",\n568:       \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the bands\",\n569:       \"footer \\\"\\\" removes the sample line; accent \\\"#b3261e\\\" recolours the hero and badge\"\n570:     ]\n571:   },\n572:   \"timeline\": {\n573:     \"source\": \"runner\",\n574:     \"phases\": [\n575:       {\n576:         \"name\": \"scout\",\n577:         \"startMs\": 0,\n578:         \"durMs\": 77498,\n579:         \"status\": \"error\"\n580:       },\n581:       {\n582:         \"name\": \"scout (2)\",\n583:         \"startMs\": 77532,\n584:         \"durMs\": 74463,\n585:         \"status\": \"error\"\n586:       },\n587:       {\n588:         \"name\": \"scout (3)\",\n589:         \"startMs\": 26271235,\n590:         \"durMs\": 147914,\n591:         \"calls\": 18,\n592:         \"tokens\": 576781,\n593:         \"costUsd\": 0.07,\n594:         \"tools\": \"bash 6, websearch 6, read 3\"\n595:       },\n596:       {\n597:         \"name\": \"plan\",\n598:         \"startMs\": 26419174,\n599:         \"durMs\": 121509,\n600:         \"calls\": 14,\n601:         \"tokens\": 480173,\n602:         \"costUsd\": 0.1,\n603:         \"tools\": \"read 12, write 2\"\n604:       }\n605:     ],\n606:     \"costBasis\": \"reported\"\n607:   },\n608:   \"caveats\": [\n609:     \"No importer: the numbers are retyped from the My Finds GPX (or a Project-GC screenshot); typeMix is JSON, not the GPX file.\",\n610:     \"Only the top five cache types render as segments; the rest and any unlisted finds fold into a grey Other remainder.\",\n611:     \"The Project-GC milestone ladder is hard-coded (1, 10, 50, 100, then hundreds to 1000, five-hundreds to 5000, thousands after).\"\n612:   ]\n613: };\n614: \n\n(Showing lines 540-614 of 683. Use offset=615 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"const WHY: WhySpec = {\n  \"day\": 31,\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n  \"agent\": \"opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-pro\",\n  \"id\": \"@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\",\n  \"title\": \"Geocache Milestone Card\",\n  \"who\": \"Geocachers hitting a milestone or building a stats card, gathered on the Geocaching forums, Project-GC, and their local clubs\",\n  \"problem\": [\n    \"Every Premium member can download their My Finds pocket query: a zipped GPX of every cache they logged. Project-GC's Milestones tab gives the ladder: 'the first milestones are 1, 10, 50 and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is considered a milestone'.\",\n    \"CacheSleuth reads the same GPX into a profile banner ('Upload your My Finds pocket query and see your geocaching statistics'), but the shareable 'I hit N finds' card is still hand-built; a local club just posts 'geohiker55 found his 1000th find yesterday'.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://www.cachesleuth.com/tools/profilestats\",\n    \"https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab\",\n    \"https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2025/05/celebrating-25-years-of-geocaching-milestones\",\n    \"https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page\",\n    \"https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\"\n  ],\n  \"solution\": [","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\variants\\a\\src\\geocache-milestone-card.ts","text":"const WHY: WhySpec = {\n  \"day\": 31,\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n  \"agent\": \"opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-pro\",\n  \"id\": \"@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\",\n  \"title\": \"Geocache Milestone Card\",\n  \"who\": \"Geocachers hitting a milestone or building a stats card, gathered on the Geocaching forums, Project-GC, and their local clubs\",\n  \"problem\": [\n    \"Every Premium member can download their My Finds pocket query: a zipped GPX of every cache they logged. Project-GC's Milestones tab gives the ladder: 'the first milestones are 1, 10, 50 and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is considered a milestone'.\",\n    \"CacheSleuth reads the same GPX into a profile banner ('Upload your My Finds pocket query and see your geocaching statistics'), but the shareable 'I hit N finds' card is still hand-built; a local club just posts 'geohiker55 found his 1000th find yesterday'.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://www.cachesleuth.com/tools/profilestats\",\n    \"https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab\",\n    \"https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2025/05/celebrating-25-years-of-geocaching-milestones\",\n    \"https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page\",\n    \"https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\"\n  ],\n  \"solution\": [\n    \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n    \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The card derives the ordinal (1,000th) and whether the count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about.\"\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @card.json -o card.png\",\n    \"try\": [\n      \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}]}\",\n      \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print it (Project-GC milestones)\",\n      \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the bands\",\n      \"footer \\\"\\\" removes the sample line; accent \\\"#b3261e\\\" recolours the hero and badge\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"timeline\": {\n    \"source\": \"runner\",\n    \"phases\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scout\",\n        \"startMs\": 0,\n        \"durMs\": 77498,\n        \"status\": \"error\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scout (2)\",\n        \"startMs\": 77532,\n        \"durMs\": 74463,\n        \"status\": \"error\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scout (3)\",\n        \"startMs\": 26271235,\n        \"durMs\": 147914,\n        \"calls\": 18,\n        \"tokens\": 576781,\n        \"costUsd\": 0.07,\n        \"tools\": \"bash 6, websearch 6, read 3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"plan\",\n        \"startMs\": 26419174,\n        \"durMs\": 121509,\n        \"calls\": 14,\n        \"tokens\": 480173,\n        \"costUsd\": 0.1,\n        \"tools\": \"read 12, write 2\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"costBasis\": \"reported\"\n  },\n  \"caveats\": [\n    \"No importer: the numbers are retyped from the My Finds GPX (or a Project-GC screenshot); typeMix is JSON, not the GPX file.\",\n    \"Only the top five cache types render as segments; the rest and any unlisted finds fold into a grey Other remainder.\",\n    \"The Project-GC milestone ladder is hard-coded (1, 10, 50, 100, then hundreds to 1000, five-hundreds to 5000, thousands after).\"\n  ]\n};\n","lineStart":540,"lineEnd":614,"totalLines":683,"truncated":true}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-20\\variants\\a\\src\\geocache-milestone-card.ts","time":{"start":1792530986505,"end":1792530986556}},"id":"prt_15b2c3469001APeTb62nGpWL9P","sessionID":"ses_ea4d52decffeaHsc6A3RWeHtGB","messageID":"msg_15b2bb06b001YKbTvNCTwhk47n"}}
