{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792531023243,"sessionID":"ses_ea4d52decffeaHsc6A3RWeHtGB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"websearch","callID":"call_00_FhmEekgNVjbAD6YbeqPq9508","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"query":"Project-GC milestones tab find count milestones every 500 1000 5000 badgegen","numResults":5},"output":"{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_8d9c0b7e2fb57b1c150501b8ba2ef874\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab\",\n      \"title\": \"Milestones tab - Project-GC\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Finds Milestones Maps FTF Events Challenges LabCaches Hides Souvenirs BadgeGen\\nMilestones tab\\nFrom Project-GC\\nJump to navigation Jump to search\\nThe Milestones tab is a tab in a user's Profile Stats . As the name suggest, this tab shows a user's milestones. This tab has four modules .\\nContents\\n* 1 Milestones\\n* 1.1 Order\\n* 1.2 Different milestones at Project-GC vs Geocaching.com\\n* 2 First cache by country\\n* 3 First cache by region in home country\\n* 4 First cache by cache type\\nMilestones\\nThe first module shows a list of the user's milestones. The first milestones are 1, 10, 50 and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is considered a milestone. Between 1000 and 5000 caches every five hundredth cache is considered a milestone, and beyond that every thousandth cache is listed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/w/BadgeGen\",\n      \"title\": \"BadgeGen - Project-GC\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"BadgeGen is included as a tab in the Profile Stats . There are 45 Badges in total, each with 8 different qualities. Most of them can also be \\\"looped\\\", ie getting \\\"double Diamond \\\" or more. Once the user have Ruby or higher they will unlock Addons .\\nExisting badges\\nRequirements\\n* Badge | Bronze | Silver | Gold | Platinum | Ruby | Sapphire | Emerald | Diamond\\n* The Achiever | 5 | 20 | 40 | 80 | 150 | 225 | 350 | 500\\n* The Adventurous Cacher | 1 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 8 | 12 | 18 | 30\\n* The All Around Cacher | 90 | 120 | 180 | 270 | 300 | 330 | 350 | 360\\n* The Attribute Cacher | 50 | 70 | 82 | 88 | 94 | 100 | 105 | 108\\n* The Event Host | 1 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 8 | 12 | 18 | 30\\n* The Favorite Cacher | 10000 | 30000 | 60000 | 100000 | 170000 | 250000 | 350000 | 500000\\n* The Favorited Owner | 25 | 40 | 60 | 90 | 150 | 210 | 320 | 500\\n* The FTF Addict | 15 | 20 | 30 | 50 | 80 | 120 | 180 | 300\\n* The Geocacher | 500 | 1000 | 2000 | 3000 | 5000 | 8000 | 12000 | 18000\\n* The Giga Social Cacher | - | 1 | 2 | - | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6\\n* The GPS Maze Cacher | - | - | 1 | 2 | 3 | - | 4 | 5\\n* The High Altitude Cacher | 500 | 1000 | 1500 | 2000 | 2500 | 3000 | 3500 | 4500\\n* The Jasmer Cacher | 36 | 72 | 144 | 216 | 285 [ 1 ] | 300 [ 1 ] | 310 [ 1 ] | 315 [ 1 ]\\n* The Lab Cacher | 10 | 25 | 50 | 100 | 200 | 400 | 600 | 800\\n* The Mega Social Cacher | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 8 | 10\\n* The Micro Cacher | 200 | 300 | 500 | 800 | 1200 | 1800 | 3000 | 4500\\n* The Multi Cacher | 50 | 100 | 200 | 300 | 500 | 800 | 1000 | 1200\\n* The Mysterious Cacher | 50 | 100 | 200 | 300 | 500 | 800 | 1200 | 1800\\n* The Odd-sized Cacher | 75 | 125 | 200 | 300 | 450 | 600 | 800 | 1200\\n* The Social Cacher | 5 | 10 | 20 | 30 | 50 | 80 | 120 | 180\\n* The Trackable Lover | 50 | 100 | 200 | 300 | 500 | 800 | 1200 | 1800\\n* The Traditional Cacher | 400 | 1000 | 2000 | 3000 | 5000 | 7000 | 10000 | 14000\\n* The Traveling Cacher | 2 | 3 | 5 | 8 | 12 | 18 | 25 | 35\\n* The Virtual Cacher | 5 | 10 | 20 | 30 | 50 | 80 | 120 | 180\\nWhen Project-GC started detailing it out more and more it became clear that some Addons will be fairly easy and others more or less impossible. The original idea was definitely aiming more for impossible than easy though. It is not meant that everyone should get every Addon, and even more so, not within a year or two.\\nBadgeGen was originally created and maintained by Kyle Mills , as a macro for GSAK. In the early days Project-GC had the license to make a similar implementation of it embedded in Project-GC. In year 2020, the ownership of BadgeGen was transferred to the owner of Project-GC.\\nKyle Mills maintained BadgeGen up until, and including, version 3.x. The new version owned by Project-GC became version 4 , plain and simple.\\nRelated: BadgeGen v3 vs v4\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/w/Main_Page\",\n      \"title\": \"Main Page - Project-GC\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"* Profile Stats\\n* Profile Stats settings\\n* Finds tab\\n* Log similarity\\n* Milestones tab\\n* Events tab\\n* FTF tab\\n* First to Find\\n* Hides tab\\n* Maps tab\\n* BadgeGen tab\\n* BadgeGen\\n* All Badges\\n* Country Badges\\n* Belts\\n* BadgeGen v3 vs v4\\n* Challenges tab\\n* Souvenirs tab\\n* LabCaches tab\\n* Progress\\n* Stat Compare\\n* Who favors who?\\nCache stats\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://cdn2.project-gc.com/\",\n      \"title\": \"Project-GC - Showroom\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Profile stats\\nCumulative finds\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by month per year\\nProfile stats\\nSome numbers\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by type/size\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by difficulty/terrain\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by month/weekday\\nProfile stats\\nPie charts\\nProfile stats\\nFinds from home\\nProfile stats\\nDifficulty terrain chart\\nProfile stats\\nWay to 81\\nProfile stats\\nBy favorite points / oldest\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by elevation\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by dates\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by owner\\nProfile stats\\nCollected attributes\\nProfile stats\\nMilestones\\nProfile stats\\nFirst cache by country/type\\nProfile stats\\nFirst to finds\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\n* Usage Data refers to data collected automatically, either generated by the use of the Service or from the Service infrastructure itself (for example, the duration of a page visit).\\n* Website refers to Project-GC, accessible from https://project-gc.com\\nRepresented by CEO/Founder Magnus Månsson\\nHeadquarters:\\nVälavägen 23-0\\n275 39 Sjöbo\\nSweden\\nContact: info@project-gc.com\\nOrganization number: 556982-2215\\nVAT number: SE556982221501\\nProject-GC\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/\",\n      \"title\": \"Project-GC - Showroom\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Please authenticate us with your Geocaching account to get access to a lot more features.\\nDid you know? (#12)\\nThat anyone can help translating Project-GC. Just visit https://translate.project-gc.com/ to get started. If your language is missing, contact support.\\nProfile stats\\nCumulative finds\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by month per year\\nProfile stats\\nSome numbers\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by type/size\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by difficulty/terrain\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by month/weekday\\nProfile stats\\nPie charts\\nProfile stats\\nFinds from home\\nProfile stats\\nDifficulty terrain chart\\nProfile stats\\nWay to 81\\nProfile stats\\nBy favorite points / oldest\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by elevation\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by dates\\nProfile stats\\nFinds by owner\\nProfile stats\\nCollected attributes\\nProfile stats\\nMilestones\\nProfile stats\\nFirst cache by country/type\\nProfile stats\\nFirst to finds\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\nHides\\nProfile stats\\n* Usage Data refers to data collected automatically, either generated by the use of the Service or from the Service infrastructure itself (for example, the duration of a page visit).\\n* Website refers to Project-GC, accessible from https://project-gc.com\\nRepresented by CEO/Founder Magnus Månsson\\nHeadquarters:\\nVälavägen 23-0\\n275 39 Sjöbo\\nSweden\\nContact: info@project-gc.com\\nOrganization number: 556982-2215\\nVAT number: SE556982221501\\nProject-GC\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2019/12/how-did-you-do-this-year-check-your-stats-with-project-gc\",\n      \"title\": \"How did you do this year? Check your stats with Project-GC – Official Blog\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"At the start of 2019, we shared an article listing 19 geocaching resolutions for 2019 . These resolutions ranged from attending an Event to filling your Difficulty and Terrain grid! Project-GC can help you keep track of these milestones and more through their dynamic statistics. So, how did you do this year and what goals do you have for 2020?\\nLooking at your profile stats is a great starting place to see how far you’ve come and what goals interest you next! Project-GC’s Profile stats are very extensive personal statistics about your finds and hides. Plus, these stats can be displayed on your Geocaching.com profile.\\nAll of these stats (and more) are available through Project-GC’s profile stats page.\\nAnd speaking of badges, check out the new progress page on Project-GC. Here you will find the answers to questions like what was your very first badge? And how have my badges evolved over time? View a personalized time-lapse on the progress page !\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/w/Badge_Statistics\",\n      \"title\": \"Badge Statistics\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Badge Statistics\\nThe sum of the percentages from Bronze->Diamond should equal ~100%. Columns to the right of the bolder line are not deducted from Diamond.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"http://www.southforkriver.net/Geo/web/stats.html\",\n      \"title\": \"Allyn56's Geocaching Statistics\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Allyn56's Geocaching Page\\nMy Statistics\\n* Allyn56's Geocaching Page\\n* |\\n* Geocaching.com\\n* |\\n* My Caches\\n* |\\n* Puzzle Caching\\n* |\\n* Current Stats\\n* Finds\\n* Milestones\\n* FTF\\n* Events\\n* Hides\\n* Maps\\n* BadgeGen\\n* Challenges\\n* Souvenirs\\n* Lab caches\\nAllyn56 has logged 17179 different geocaches,\\nincluding 473 lab caches\\nProject-GC stats\\nData from 2026-01-01\\nCumulative finds by month\\nCumulative finds by month\\nIncluding 473 lab caches\\nFinds by month per year\\n2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 2016 2015 2014 2013 2012 2011 2010 2009 2008 2007 2006 All\\n2025\\n112\\n73\\n89\\n80\\n35\\n72\\n39\\n31\\n24\\n64\\n31\\n25\\n* Total finds | 675\\n* Days caching | 97\\n* Average finds per caching day | 7.0\\n* Overall finds per day | 1.9\\n* Overall finds per month | 56.3\\nMonth:\\nJan\\nFeb\\nMar\\nApr\\nMay\\nJun\\nJul\\nAug\\nSep\\nOct\\nNov\\nDec\\nDays caching:\\n9\\n4\\n11\\n13\\n10\\n9\\n7\\n7\\n6\\n5\\n8\\n8\\nIncluding 222 lab caches\\n2024\\n12\\n57\\n405\\n62\\n45\\n44\\n20\\n69\\n23\\n38\\n192\\n55\\n* Total finds | 1022\\n* Days caching | 85\\n* Average finds per caching day | 12.0\\n* Overall finds per day | 2.8\\n* Overall finds per month | 85.2\\nMonth:\\nJan\\nFeb\\nMar\\nApr\\nMay\\nJun\\nJul\\nAug\\nSep\\nOct\\nNov\\nDec\\nDays caching:\\n6\\n6\\n11\\n8\\n7\\n5\\n5\\n7\\n3\\n9\\n9\\n9\\nIncluding 100 lab caches\\nSome numbers\\n* Overall total finds: | 17179 finds in 1593 caching days over 7260 total days (21.9%) 2\\n* Fastest 100 finds: | 1 day on 2011-08-27 2\\n* Last 100 finds: | 64 days 2\\n* Fastest 1000 finds: | 43 days from 2012-02-24 to 2012-04-06 2\\n* Last 1000 finds: | 496 days 2\\n* Total cache-to-cache distance: | 325,003 km, 8.11 x earth circumnavigation, 0.845 x distance to the moon 1\\n* Maximum distance in a day: | 8,732 km, 12 geocaches, on 2011-03-12 1\\n* CITO | 28 | 0.16% |\\n* L&F Event | 10 | 0.06% |\\n* Locationless | 2 | 0.01% |\\nIncluding 473 lab caches\\nFinds by size\\n* Type | Amount | Percent\\n* Micro | 11491 | 68.78% |\\n* Small | 3190 | 19.09% |\\n* Regular | 902 | 5.40% |\\n* Other | 650 | 3.89% |\\n* Not chosen | 334 | 2.00% |\\n* Virtual | 90 | 0.54% |\\n* Large | 49 | 0.29% |\\nFinds by difficulty rating\\n* Elevation | < 0 | < 25 | < 50 | < 75 | < 100 | < 125 | < 150 | < 200 | < 250 | < 300 | < 400 | < 500 | < 600 | < 750 | < 1000 | < 1250 | < 1500 | < 1750 | < 2000 | < 2500 | ≥ 2500\\nFinds by found date\\n* Type: - | Date | Size: -\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://project-gc.com/w/The_Favorite_Cacher\",\n      \"title\": \"The Favorite Cacher\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"The Favorite Cacher\\nMay 31, 2023 — Sum the favorite points of every Geocache. When that sum reaches 10,000, the user earns their Bronze medal; at 500,000, their Diamond Gembadge.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"http://github.itlym.cn/bertuko/GC/milestones\",\n      \"title\": \"Milestones · bertuko/GC · GitHub\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Skip to content ## Navigation Menu\\n* Issues\\n* Assigned to me\\n* Created by me\\n* Mentioned\\n* Recent activity\\n* Projects\\n* Milestones\\n* Labels\\n* Feedback Preview\\n* Collapse sidebar\\nMilestones\\nList view\\n* Open 0 (0)\\n* Closed 0 (0)\\n  Sort\\nYou haven’t created any Milestones.\\nUse Milestones to create collections of Issues and Pull Requests for a particular release or project.\\nFooter\\n© 2026 GitHub, Inc.\\nFooter navigation\\n* Terms\\n* Privacy\\n* Security\\n* Status\\n* Community\\n* Docs\\n* Contact\\n* Manage cookies\\n* Do not share my personal information\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea4d52decffeaHsc6A3RWeHtGB\"\n}","metadata":{"provider":"parallel","truncated":false},"title":"Parallel Web Search: Project-GC milestones tab find count milestones every 500 1000 5000 badgegen","time":{"start":1792531022676,"end":1792531023240}},"id":"prt_1